From 7eb3359b10a63bf01a45bfdd4f6040d73928acc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:22:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Texture quality: Off, Low, Medium and High replace the
 Quality preset

The menu's Quality row set the resolution, the HD textures and the HD text together. It is gone: Resolution and the HD text have rows of
their own, and "Texture quality" sets how big the HD pack's images are, against the game's own textures (1x): Off draws the game's own
textures, Low the HD ones at 1x, Medium at 2x, High as the pack stores them.

It is done in the game, with no extra files: a bundle image (BC7, with its smaller sizes stored in it) starts at the smallest stored size
that is still as big as asked, a PNG is halved as often as that allows, and a GPU without BC7 decodes that level. Nothing is made larger,
nor smaller than asked. The setting is video.texture_size (1, 2, or 0 as stored; the environment variable <PREFIX>_TEXTURE_SIZE). Changing
it loads the images again.
